[ ] Move the SHACL shapes and JSON-LD context into the spec; the ontology keeps only meaning $Decided 2026-09-30 with the human: shapes are a schema, not an ontology, and other users of the ontology may want different shapes. Move ontology/v4/actions-shapes-v4.ttl and actions.context.json into specifications/schemas beside the JSON schemas, with their tests; repoint specifications/ontology.md (which today names ontology/v4/* canonical). Delete ontology/v4/actions.schema.json: it is a stale second copy (2026-08-18, its own \$id) of the spec's pinned actions.schema.json, and the two differ. Independent of the v5 domain work; v4 data is what Core emits today. Shapes live in the spec, not the CLI (decided 2026-09-30): the CLI implements the projection and tests its output against the spec's shapes, as Core already does for the JSON schemas, so any second implementation has the same contract. Only shape-testing examples move; meaning-testing examples stay in the ontology for the ROBOT gate.$ !2 ^2026-09-30T21:55 #01a0f5d0-ebb2-73bd-a381-d8e4ae301f9c
[ ] Gate the ontology with ROBOT\: reason over the ontology plus every valid example $Found 2026-09-30 with ROBOT 1.9.10 + HermiT: v4 plus examples/v4/valid/action-sequential-chain.ttl is INCONSISTENT, and no check noticed. Two causes: (1) cco:is_successor_of has domain and range independent continuant, but v4 links actions with it; (2) v4 uses is_a_nominal_measurement_of backwards (action -> status), which makes the action itself a measurement. BFO makes independent and generically dependent continuants disjoint. Reproduce: robot merge --catalog v4/catalog-v001.xml --input v4/actions-vocabulary.owl --input <example> --output m.owl; robot explain --input m.owl --reasoner HermiT -M inconsistency --explanation e.md. Caution: chaining merge and reason in one robot command produced output with no error; reason over the merged file in a separate step. Replaces hand-vendored imports/ with robot-managed ones pinned to CCO v2.2. SCOPE (decided 2026-09-30 with the human): ROBOT is the ontology's only test tool. reason over the ontology plus the examples that test MEANING (these stay in the ontology repo: realistic plans, steps and records that must not contradict BFO/CCO); robot query runs each competency question in ontology/V5_DESIGN.md as SPARQL against those examples; robot verify fails on must-never-happen queries; robot report lints. Examples that test SHAPE move to the spec with the SHACL shapes. The ontology's Python tests (pyshacl, pytest) retire; tasks.py (website) is a separate question.$ !2 ^2026-09-30T21:59 #01a0f5d4-c03c-71b5-ad32-5befd2bfc86d
[ ] File the CCO term request for Action Specification $FOR THE HUMAN. Draft is ontology/upstream/cco-new-term-action-specification.md, in CCO's own term-request format; no duplicate upstream (searched 2026-09-30). Recommended: file it as is from your GitHub account (public, in your name). If CCO adopts it, v5 swaps IAO_0000007 for the CCO IRI and the ontology references CCO alone for actions.$ !3 +human ^2026-09-30T23:17 #01a0f61c-a851-7216-92f5-0ce16e9c5c2c
